# Technical Documentation

Requirements describe WHAT the project must accomplish. Technical documents describe HOW implementation, configuration, and operations work. ADRs describe WHY consequential decisions were made.

## Index

| Document | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [00-coding-standards.md](00-coding-standards.md) | Naming conventions, lint/format tooling, design patterns, chosen libraries |
| [01-documentation-conventions.md](01-documentation-conventions.md) | Markdown status headers, documentation levels, sprawl control |
| [05-implementation-index.md](05-implementation-index.md) | Current implementation inventory, code locations, validation commands, known gaps |
| [25-documentation-authority.md](25-documentation-authority.md) | Documentation ownership, reading order, changelog discipline |

Numbering leaves gaps (00, 01, 05, 25, ...) so new topic documents can be inserted later without renumbering existing ones.

Informal write-ups that aren't implementation guides belong in [../discussions/](../discussions/) instead of here.

## Implementation Status

Use [05-implementation-index.md](05-implementation-index.md) to answer "what exists in code now?", "where did we leave off?", and "what's the next gap?" Requirements documents should not each grow their own implementation-status section — that duplication goes stale.
